   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Idol: image to 3D gaussian splat\n\n[Idol](https://huggingface.co/speridlabs/idol) by Speridlabs is the TripoSplat architecture retrained, so ComfyUI runs it natively on the stock TripoSplat nodes. This pack adds the converted weights, **Idol Preprocess Image** (Idol's crop modes, background removal in place) and **Idol Camera** (the input camera the model predicts).\n\n**Models** (put each in the folder shown)\n\n| File | Folder | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idol_fp16.safetensors` | `models/diffusion_models` | [nynxz/Idol](https://huggingface.co/nynxz/Idol) |\n| `idol_decoder_fp16.safetensors` | `models/vae` | [nynxz/Idol](https://huggingface.co/nynxz/Idol) |\n| `dino_v3_vit_h.safetensors` | `models/clip_vision` | [VAST-AI/TripoSplat](https://huggingface.co/VAST-AI/TripoSplat/tree/main/clip_vision) |\n| `flux2-vae.safetensors` | `models/vae` | [VAST-AI/TripoSplat](https://huggingface.co/VAST-AI/TripoSplat/tree/main/vae) |\n| `birefnet.safetensors` | `models/background_removal` | [Comfy-Org/BiRefNet](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/BiRefNet/tree/main/background_removal) |\n\n**Settings**\n\n- Idol Preprocess Image `mode`: **synthetic** for renders / generated images (the object fills 1/1.2 of the frame), **real** for photographs (1/1.7).\n- KSampler: `euler` / `simple`, **50** steps, cfg **4.0** = Idol's defaults (cfg_strength 3 + time shift 3, which the model config carries). `dpmpp_2m` at 20 steps is a faster trade-off.\n- TripoSplat Decode `num_gaussians`: 262144 matches the octree's density; more oversamples the same points.\n- **Idol Prune Splat** drops the near-transparent gaussians (about half of them) that the 3D viewer and exports draw as a fuzzy halo. `min_opacity` 0.05 is a good default; `max_scale` 0.05 also removes needle-shaped spikes.\n- The top Render Splat shows the splat from the camera Idol predicted for the input, so it should look like the preprocessed image. The bottom one is a turntable.\n"
   ],
   "title": "Idol"
  }
